<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine deputies approve sale of mortgage bank.</title>
<headline>Argentine deputies approve sale of mortgage bank.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina's Chamber of Deputies passed late Wednesday &quot;in detail&quot; a bill to privatize the national mortgage bank, from which the government expects to raise $3.0-3.5 billion.</p>
<p>Last week the deputies passed the bill &quot;in general terms.&quot;</p>
<p>The bill has now completed all the necessary stages in the lower house of Congress and will now go to the Senate. Analysts see Senate approval as a foregone conclusion due to the strong majority held by the Peronist Party of President Carlos Menem.</p>
<p>((--Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 318-0650))</p>
